A||N||3||stimpy||Did I destroy my alternator?||||4||
Z||000000||stimpy||04-08-2001||02:39 PM||||Last weekend I threw my alternator/water pump belt. I went to O'Reilly's where the clerk sold me a 5 rib belt. Well, I did my best to put it on, but couldn't get it all the way on. I limped the car home and found that theoutside rib of the belt was worn off, and the alternator wasn't charging. Question is this. Did the sidewayys force on the pulleys have some detrimental effect on my alteranator, or my water pump? Help me Mr. Wizard!<BR>||||reg||4
Z||000001||Taijiguy||04-08-2001||02:58 PM||||Dunno how far you drove it, but my gut reaction is "nah". It seems to me any damage you would have done would be mechanical, and you'd be hearing those things making a racket. Maybe you just pulled a connector apart trying to get the belt on. <BR>~Taiji||||reg||1
Z||000002||hugh||04-08-2001||03:15 PM||||Taiji is right.If it's not charging now and it was before then you probably knocked a wire loose.The overtight belt can hurt the bearings,so if the belt is off now just spin the alternator and water pump by hand.If they sound ok and you can't move them sideways they are ok.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wolfhound||04-08-2001||09:17 PM||||The first belt may have disconnected something when it came apart also.||||reg||1
